# Vera Faith Experience

Experimental interactive music-themed developer portfolio. Feel like a futuristic private listening room / record archive — not a conventional website.

Human-facing brand: **Vera Faith**. Internal slug / package id: **vera-faith**.

## Visual language
- Black / near-black base; deep cherry red accents; warm amber/orange lighting
- Chrome/metallic details, smoked glass, subtle film grain + vinyl texture, soft bloom/reflections
- Sophisticated editorial typography; Japanese graphic design influence where appropriate
- Premium music-equipment / museum-installation aesthetic
- Avoid: generic SaaS, floating rounded cards, excessive gradients, template looks

## Interaction (primary)
Everything should react when appropriate: cursor, drag, scroll velocity, hover, click, camera parallax, inertia, springs, lighting, audio state. Animations need physical weight and momentum.

## Portfolio model
Projects = unique vinyl + sleeve. Browse collection → select → sleeve to turntable → vinyl slides out → lands → spins → tonearm lowers → project song plays → UI becomes liner notes/visuals.

## Intro
Cinematic close-up of record player in darkness; large vinyl + suspended tonearm; CTA **"DROP THE NEEDLE"**. On click: init audio → lower tonearm → spin → crackle/intro → camera into groove → tunnel/waveform → emerge into listening room.

## Tech & architecture
- Next.js App Router, TypeScript, Tailwind, Motion (`motion/react`), Three.js, R3F, Drei, Zustand
- Long-form text + a11y-critical UI in HTML; R3F for environmental 3D/spatial interaction; Motion for DOM UI
- Data-driven project content — do not tightly couple projects to visual components
- Desktop spectacular; mobile simplified; respect `prefers-reduced-motion`; usability over spectacle
- Avoid unnecessary deps and monolithic components; strong TypeScript

## Implementation checklist
1. Inspect existing architecture
2. Plan fit within the experience
3. Implement cleanly
4. Run lint/build
5. Fix errors before declaring done
